          "severity": "High",
          "area": "Undercut/3D flange geometry",
          "description": "32 undercut faces relative to the draw direction indicate flanges or tabs that cannot be formed in a single straight-pull stamping motion.",
          "impact": "Requires cam-driven secondary stations or multiple die sets, increasing progressive die cost beyond baseline estimate.",
          "fix": "Reorient the part or split into two stamped sub-assemblies joined by spot-welding/riveting to eliminate undercuts."
        },
        {
          "severity": "Medium",
          "area": "Minimum wall/gauge 0.53mm",
          "description": "Localised thin sections near 0.5mm are near the practical minimum for HSS stamping without splitting at tight bend radii.",
          "impact": "Risk of cracking at bend lines, increasing scrap rate and press downtime for die maintenance.",
          "fix": "Increase bend radius to >=1x material thickness at thin sections or locally thicken via tailor-welded blank."
        },
        {
          "severity": "Medium",
          "area": "Threaded/fastener feature",
          "description": "A threaded feature is not natively produced by blanking/bending and needs a secondary or in-die fastener insertion process.",
          "impact": "Adds secondary operation cost and cycle time (~0.5min/feature) plus fastener piece cost.",
          "fix": "Add in-die self-piercing nut (SPN) station to eliminate a separate secondary operation."
